Z||000000||mikemrq||06-14-2001||07:51 PM||||I have a '86 fiero 4sp v6. I called Aamco transmissions and they said they can do it for about $600.00. But the place they get the clutch said the fiero clutches come back defective. Not because the clutch is bad, but the fiero has many problems that cause the clutch to go bad quick, such as a bad master cylinder, slave cylinder, and or a cracked fork. They said all this would have to be looked at and the company may not want to send the fiero clutch being afraid it will become defective. Is this a line of BULL! or should i take it to someone else?||||reg||1
Z||000001||EdsB52||06-14-2001||08:00 PM||||This is their way of saying "Fiero clutch jobs are a whore and we would rather not do them." Look, you can do it in a weekend, so how much is your time worth? You drive an 86 4speed Fiero, you can't be a millionaire, why don't you do it yourself. ||||reg||1
